    {
      "fullUrl": "DocumentReference/model-card-acme-clinical-text",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "DocumentReference",
        "id": "model-card-acme-clinical-text",
        "meta": {
          "profile": [
            "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/aitransparency/StructureDefinition/AI-ModelCard"
          ]
        },
        "identifier": [
          {
            "system": "http://example.org/ai-vendor/model-cards",
            "value": "acme-clinical-text-foundation-model-1.0.0.md"
          }
        ],
        "status": "current",
        "type": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/aitransparency/CodeSystem/AIinputsCS",
              "code": "AIModelCard"
            }
          ]
        },
        "category": [
          {
            "coding": [
              {
                "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/aitransparency/CodeSystem/AIinputsCS",
                "code": "AIModelCardMarkdownFormat",
                "display": "Markdown Format"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "description": "# Acme Clinical Text Foundation Model\n\n> Synthetic connectathon model card. This document describes dummy test data and\n> does not represent a production clinical model.\n\n## Model identity\n\n- **Model family:** Acme Clinical Text Foundation Model\n- **Model role:** Shared language model used by the ScribeAssist LLM and\n  TextXtract NLP Pipeline devices\n- **Model-card version:** 1.0.0\n- **Provider:** Acme Clinical AI, Inc.\n- **Related Devices:** `Device/ai-device-1` and `Device/ai-device-2`\n\n## Intended use\n\nThe model supports clinical-document summarization and extraction of explicitly\nstated observations, allergy information, and medication information from\nclinical text. It is intended to assist trained healthcare professionals and\ndata-processing workflows. It is not intended to diagnose, triage, prescribe,\nor make autonomous clinical decisions.\n\n## Training and evaluation data\n\nThis synthetic card does not claim a real training or evaluation dataset.\nConnectathon resources are fictional and are used only to exercise FHIR\nprovenance, model-card, and transparency workflows.\n\n## Limitations and risks\n\nThe model may omit, misinterpret, or incorrectly structure information from\nclinical text. Performance may vary with writing style, specialty, language,\nabbreviations, and missing context. Outputs require review by a qualified\nhuman before clinical use, and generated content must not be treated as an\nindependent source of truth.\n\n## Oversight and change management\n\nDeployments should record the device and version used for each AI-assisted\nresource in FHIR Provenance. Changes to the underlying model, prompts, or\nprocessing pipeline should receive a new model-card version and be evaluated\nbefore production use.\n",
        "content": [
          {
            "attachment": {
              "contentType": "text/markdown",
              "data": ""
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "url": "DocumentReference/model-card-acme-clinical-text"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "DocumentReference/model-card-acme-earlywarn-risk",
